      "name": "Fregata",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "The sole genus of the family, comprising five species of large, lightly built seabirds instantly recognisable by their deeply forked tails, long hooked bills, and the male's inflatable red throat pouch. Frigatebirds are masters of aerial piracy, harrying other seabirds to force them to disgorge their catch.",
