          "commonName": "Magnificent frigatebird",
          "lineage": "Frigatebirds",
          "continents": [
            "North America",
            "South America"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The magnificent frigatebird, frigate petrel or man o' war is a seabird of the frigatebird family Fregatidae. With a length of 89–114 centimetres and wingspan of 2.17–2.44 m, it is the largest species of frigatebird. It occurs over tropical and subtropical waters off America, between northern Mexico and Peru on the Pacific coast and between Florida and southern Brazil along the Atlantic coast.",
